## Why This Is Asked

Examines practical handling of delayed supervision, distribution drift, and safe deployment in production ML systems.

## Key Concepts

- Delayed feedback and label latency
- Concept drift and drift detectors (ADWIN-like)
- Online vs offline retraining
- Calibration and evaluation (AUROC, PR-AUC, FPR)
- Data/versioning and deployment safety

## Code Example

```javascript
// Implementation sketch
let model = initModel();
let buffer = [];
stream.on('event', async (e) => {
  const x = featuresFromEvent(e);
  const yHat = model.predict(x);
  storePrediction(e.id, yHat);
  buffer.push({id: e.id, x, timestamp: Date.now()});
});

// Drift detection
setInterval(() => {
  const recent = getRecentPredictions(window);
  const metrics = evaluateMetrics(recent);
  if (driftDetector.detect(metrics)) {
    triggerOfflineRetrain();
  }
}, 3600000);
```

## Why This Is Asked
Assess ability to design scalable, tenant-aware ML pipelines with calibration, streaming features, drift handling, and safe rollout strategies across enterprise-scale tenants.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-tenant feature stores and leakage prevention
- Shared base model + per-tenant calibrator
- Real-time features from streaming usage and billing
- Online retraining with drift detectors
- Offline + online evaluation and staged rollout

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo calibration hook
function calibrate(probs, tenantId, store){
  const params = store.getParams(tenantId)
  // adjust by temp scaler
  return Math.min(0.999, Math.max(0.001, probs * params.scale + params.bias))
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate per-tenant calibration offline and online?
- How would you guard against cross-tenant data leakage in CV and feature drift?

## Why This Is Asked
