## Why This Is Asked
A beginner-safe way to ensure models stay reliable in production, focusing on data drift and quick retraining.

## Key Concepts
- Data drift vs concept drift
- KS statistic, rolling window evaluation
- Lightweight retraining, canary/shadow deployment
- Feature versioning and rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// drift check scaffold (pseudo)
function ksTest(a, b) { /* returns p-value */ }
function driftFeatures(train, prod, thresh=0.05) {
  const drift = {};
  for (const key of Object.keys(train)) {
    drift[key] = ksTest(train[key], prod[key]);
  }
  return Math.max(...Object.values(drift)) < thresh;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you set thresholds for drift in a new product line?
- How would you extend this to multiclass targets or time-series features?

## Why This Is Asked

Production ML systems must adapt to concept drift and data skew without sacrificing stability. This question probes concrete, actionable strategies beyond theory.

## Key Concepts

- Concept drift detection
- Sliding window retraining
- Score calibration and monitoring
- Safe deployment and rollback

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal drift check sketch (conceptual)
function detectDrift(scores, windowSize, threshold) {
  const w = scores.slice(-windowSize);
  const mean = w.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0)/w.length;
  return Math.abs(mean - 0.5) > threshold;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate the rollback path before production deployment?
- Which telemetry would you collect to prove drift handling works?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical baseline ML for streaming signals with delayed labels, focusing on CPU constraints and simple online learning.

## Key Concepts
- Online updates with partial_fit
- Drift detection (PSI/KS)
- Calibration (Platt scaling)
- Simple retraining cadence and data splits

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: batch online update loop
function onlineUpdate(batch){
  model.partial_fit(batch.features, batch.labels);
  monitorDrift(batch.features);
  calibrateIfNeeded();
}
```

